  "id": "10877_yudaneru",
  "headword": "{委|ゆだ}ねる",
  "reading": "ゆだねる",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to entrust, to leave to",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to entrust, to leave to, to delegate",
      "explanation": "To place a matter, decision, or responsibility in someone else's hands, trusting them to handle it."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10877_yudaneru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{判断|はんだん}を{彼|かれ}に{委|ゆだ}ねた。",
      "english": "I left the decision to him.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10877_yudaneru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{運命|うんめい}に{身|み}を{委|ゆだ}ねる。",
      "english": "To resign oneself to fate.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10877_yudaneru_ex3",
      "japanese": "この{問題|もんだい}は{専門家|せんもんか}に{委|ゆだ}ねたほうがいい。",
      "english": "It would be better to leave this matter to the experts.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Pattern: XをYに{委|ゆだ}ねる.\n\nUSAGE:\nA somewhat formal verb often used in written language and formal speech. The thing entrusted (decision, fate, responsibility) is marked with を, and the person or entity receiving it is marked with に.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {判断|はんだん}を{委|ゆだ}ねる: to leave the judgment to\n- {運命|うんめい}に{身|み}を{委|ゆだ}ねる: to entrust oneself to fate\n- {決定|けってい}を{委|ゆだ}ねる: to delegate a decision\n- {裁量|さいりょう}に{委|ゆだ}ねる: to leave to someone's discretion\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{任|まか}せる is more conversational and broadly used. {委|ゆだ}ねる carries a more formal, literary tone and often implies a deeper level of trust or resignation.",
